Phase 6 continuation, 2026-10-09. Pinned Java source remains read-only at efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9.

Assignment-mode probe commit beb6fe7 adds the exact decimal input `0.9999999999999999999`. The pinned Java decoder returns PULL after exact truncation; before the fix the native f64 path rounded this value to 1.0 and returned POP. A second oracle case shows decimal `4294967296.0` wraps to PULL, while the plain integer `4294967296` rejects. Probe commit 21d5b70 adds the integer-versus-decimal distinction.

Implementation commit dcc822b decodes mode values from raw JSON tokens and routes numeric values through the shared Fastjson-compatible i32 conversion. The focused mode differential passes all 20 cases. The implementation and probes remain in separate commits.

Fixture inventory: route DTO inputs 80, SHA-256 74ad05fe746f63b1b4fd5886d3fd135a60a4f252fd7ea037e6d4a420fedc4e12; lookup assignment-mode inputs 20, consumer-list inputs 13, assignment-attachment inputs seven, SHA-256 42a05d175175b94dc7e1bfc051940f70b16a01cbba0345ff2a35a5a0fa2d57e1; heartbeat DTO inputs 52, SHA-256 e183f318134bd5dfa85bcbd80276c3e85c444f3ca0ebbe8231696ef2b4305db7.

Validation passed: all 75 protocol tests; full `cargo test --workspace --all-targets --locked --quiet`; strict all-target/all-feature Clippy; pinned offline Maven verify with deterministic fixture regeneration (22 scenarios); `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; and `git diff --check`. No Broker, Docker, live server, deployment, plan, or pinned Java source was modified. Phase 6 remains incomplete; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.

API-map count reconciliation, 2026-10-09. Corrected the current detailed lookup DTO rows to match their accepted evidence: consumer-list input cases 12→13, assignment-mode cases 17→20, and assignment-attachment cases 6→7. The assignment response Set row remains 12 because it is the separate ADR-0019 corpus. `git diff --check` passes. Full Phase 6 API/source/input reconciliation and the final-plan audit remain open; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.

Fresh Phase 6 gate rerun, 2026-10-09: the plan's `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --test runtime --locked` passed 13/13; `cargo test --workspace --all-targets --locked` passed; strict `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` passed; `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` passed and validated 22 scenarios; comparator self-test and 22-scenario manifest validation passed; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` passed. The first sandboxed runtime/Maven attempts were denied loopback binding and the local Maven artifact lock; the same authorized test commands passed when rerun with required access. The Java artifact remained pinned to client 5.5.1 and contacted no Broker. These gates do not close the remaining source/API/input audit; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.

Endpoint port probe, 2026-10-09. The pinned Java 5.5.1 `NettyRemotingClient.getHostAndPort`/`Integer.parseInt` fixture now has 21 client endpoint cases. It confirms BMP Arabic-Indic, Fullwidth, mixed ASCII/Unicode, and Devanagari decimal digits parse as ports; negative values, values above 65535, i32 overflow, and a supplementary mathematical digit reject. The native `address_splitting_matches_pinned_java_last_colon_oracle` regression failed before implementation at `127.0.0.1:١٠٩١١` (`Address::parse` rejected while Java accepted 10911). Probe/test changes are in a separate commit from the forthcoming parser fix. Fixture SHA-256 `4a408974a90cbdafb535cd81fe29a0e4d1d3264f3a8379e8a6228e78156e0053`.

Endpoint port differential/fix, 2026-10-09. Oracle/test commit `c8d0171` extends `fixtures/runtime/address.json` to 21 direct Java endpoint splits, records `Integer.parseInt` values, and adds BMP Arabic-Indic/fullwidth/mixed/Devanagari digits plus negative, >65535, i32-overflow, and supplementary mathematical-digit cases. The focused native differential failed before implementation at Arabic-Indic 10911. Fix `51cef1d` adds a private Java UTF-16 `Character.digit` i32 parser and applies it in both `Address::parse` and `connection::split_address`, with Java socket-port range validation. The regression passes; address fixture SHA-256 `4a408974a90cbdafb535cd81fe29a0e4d1d3264f3a8379e8a6228e78156e0053`.

Post-fix validation passed: focused address differential, full `cargo test --workspace --all-targets --locked`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`, pinned offline Maven verify (22 scenarios, including 21 endpoint cases), comparator self-test, 22-scenario manifest validation, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and `git diff --check`. No Broker/Docker was contacted. Other address/transport families and whole Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.

Inbound property-record differential/fix, 2026-10-09. The pinned Java 5.5.1 `MessageDecoder.string2messageProperties` oracle adds nine cases to `fixtures/runtime/inbound-routing.json`: empty-valued records, empty duplicates after a valid value, valid duplicate overwrite, embedded name/value separators, empty keys, and a supplementary key. Java ignores empty keys/values; a later empty duplicate therefore leaves its prior nonempty value. The focused Rust differential failed before the fix at `PGROUP\u0001\u0002`, where Rust retained `PGROUP=""`. Oracle/test commit `0041553` and fixture SHA-256 `534f1d4be1d82abd4c9d18c11265dae4445344cb434c7483f55874f3f7d25669`; implementation commit `df63dae` changes only the permissive wire parser condition and its prior empty-value assertion. The focused parser tests pass. The first sandboxed workspace run was blocked by loopback permission; the same full locked workspace suite passed with authorized socket access. Strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, pinned offline Maven verify (22 scenarios; eight binary routing cases plus nine property inputs), comparator self-test/manifest22, fmt and diff checks passed. No Broker/Docker was contacted. Full Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remains open, and P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.

Manager first-runtime source alignment, 2026-10-09. Pinned Java bytecode for `MQClientManager.getOrCreateMQClientInstance` performs table `get`, then clones config and invokes `computeIfAbsent` only for an absent client ID. A direct actual manager fixture now proves later same-ID calls with changed NameServer, namespaceV2, TLS and timeout return the same runtime, preserve the first config, and do not mutate the later caller. Before-fix test `p6_v02_same_client_id_reuses_first_java_manager_runtime` failed with `RuntimeError::ConfigurationConflict`; oracle/test commit `204de99`, client-config fixture SHA-256 `54ac6d1c912a19ee61f660a427969fb3e5e9b61656f57a03ffd4654bc30cff63`. Fix `b18771d` removes config/property/hook conflict checks and the now-unreachable public error; only first insertion captures configuration, construction properties and hook. Manager-table and namespace/stream collision regressions also pass. Full locked workspace/all-targets, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, pinned offline Maven verify (22 scenarios), comparator self-test/manifest22, fmt and diff checks passed. No Broker/Docker was contacted. This supersedes the former native-only conflict policy recorded in ADR-0004; whole Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remains open, and P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.

Inbound RPC-hook boundary audit, 2026-10-09. Pinned 5.5.1 `MQClientAPIImpl` registers `ClientRemotingProcessor` through `RemotingClient.registerProcessor`; generic `NettyRemotingAbstract.buildProcessRequestHandler` calls before hooks, request pipeline, processor, and after hooks in that order. Thus inbound broker commands do pass through RPC hooks. Rust `client/processor.rs::process_registered` has the same ordering; no change/test was warranted for this candidate. Recorded in `docs/compatibility/PHASE_6_INBOUND_MATRIX.md`. Broader Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remains open; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.

Route DTO property-name input audit, 2026-10-09. Added four direct pinned Fastjson 2.0.63 cases for uppercase, title-case, snake-case, and duplicate case-variant `QueueData` field names. Java accepts the JSON but leaves fields at defaults in each case; Rust Serde does the same. The first native run exposed the stale 80-case inventory assertion; after the fixture/test update all 84 route DTO input cases pass. Oracle/test commit `7985ef7`; current route fixture SHA-256 `fbd41914d362bee3e1293c1b23ac5ea88d1c0d2e33237f6aaaf07d10c1234b27`. Maven compile and direct route fixture generation succeeded; focused `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol route_dto_inputs_match_invoked_java_fastjson --locked` passed. No implementation change was warranted. Full Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remains open; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.
